{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm]Come along, catch a [Fm]Heffalump,
[Cm]Sit with me on a [Fm]muddy clump,
[Cm]We'll sing a song of [G]days gone [Cm]by.
[Cm]Run along now, [Fm]don’t be glum,
[Cm]Get you gone, now, [Fm]have some fun,
[Cm]Don't be long, for the [G]end is [Cm]nigh.
[Fm]Don't let [Eb]moments [Fm]pass [Eb]along
[Fm]And waste [Eb]before your [G]eyes;
[Cm]March with me and the [Fm]borogoves,
[Cm]Come with me and the [Fm]slithy toves,
[Cm]And never [G]ask us [Cm]why.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
